    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Total nr of beneficiaries disaggregated by Male/Female and Domestic/school/public users Please also check the criteria per service level to see what level best matches your initiative. The initiative must fulfill all criteria to be considered at that service level. 1. Safely managed service: 2. the initiative provides an improved source of water (this includes: piped water, boreholes or tube wells, protected dug wells, protected springs, rainwater, packaged / bottled water, water that is delivered) 3. the initiative is located on the premises of the household or dwelling 4. the initiative provides drinking water whenever it is needed 5. the drinking water provided by the initiative has no presence of E.coli 6. the drinking water provided by the initiative contains no / limited levels of arsenic and fluoride (below WHO standards: &lt; 0.01 mg/L arsenic and &lt; 1.5mg/L fluoride 7. Basic service: 8. the initiative provides an improved source of water (this includes: piped water, boreholes or tube wells, protected dug wells, protected springs, rainwater, packaged / bottled water, water that is delivered) 9. the initiative provides water for users where the collection time is less than 30 minutes for a roundtrip including queuing 0. Limited service: Drinking water from an improved source for which collection time exceeds 30 minutes for a roundtrip including queuing. 1. Unimproved service: Drinking water from an unprotected dug well or unprotected spring \* This is indicative of the reach and scale of the initiative in reaching new users with its products and services in terms of the service level that is being provided (as defined by JMP).</narrative>
